{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/601843-biological-sex-and-the-mask","id":601843,"title":"Biological sex and the Mask","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-24T08:31:49-07:00","id":601843,"title":"Biological sex and the Mask","content":"Hoooo. Okay, once again, starting a thread here very, very nervously. Different reasons this time - less unfamiliarity (you guys seem pretty cool?) and more... slightly ashamed of the subject matter.<br /> <br /> So it's clearly possible for a Changeling to no longer have a biological sex. Being made entirely of snow, or being a tree, or so on results in a Changeling who in spite of their Mask does not have a sex in any human fashion. This doesn't TEND to bleed through the mask, because... the mask is obviously human. So the mask appears to have the biological sex of the Changeling beforehand.<br /> <br /> As a contrast to that, their fae Mien clearly does affect their mask in some ways - Wizened may appear shorter or 'lessened', and Ogre masks adapt to their new hulking forms, resulting in a Changeling who is noticibly different from themselves pre-abduction.<br /> <br /> I've been wondering (and beating myself up over - as mentioned, ashamed that I'm asking about this) - if a Keeper was to change the sex of one of their Changelings, which is undeniably within their power in Arcadia and seems pretty plausible for someone taken as a Romancer - and they escaped, would their Mask be identical to themselves pre-abduction, or would it be like an Ogre, adapting slightly to fit the new form?<br /> <br /> The Bodhisattvas of the Broken Cage are noted to occasionally slowly change sex. This, however, doesn't affect their mask at all. Is this just a hard-and-fast rule on the Mask always conforming to their gender identity, or is their mask trying to... well, mask the changes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6848-taveena","name":"Taveena","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T08:40:10-07:00","id":601869,"title":"","content":"Something to be said about the Mask that is mentioned but isn't prominent is that the Mask molds to what makes sense as a human analogue to the faerie under it. So, let's say I got taken and got turned into a woman. Coming back, I would find that my Mask looks like a female version of myself, like I went got a really good sex change operation.<br /> <br /> The Mask is rigid, but it's not so rigid as to be completely contradictory. The example they gave in the book was if someone went and lost a lot of weight in Arcadia, the weight loss would show, just not anything related to the fae. Gender goes the same way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T09:33:22-07:00","id":601914,"title":"","content":"That's basically what I thought, but given the Bodhisattvas I wasn't sure. Any thoughts on why they're different?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6848-taveena","name":"Taveena","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T09:40:59-07:00","id":601917,"title":"","content":"This is a situation where I believe the kind of story the player is trying to tell with this character is infinitely more important than anything written in the book. Does the player want to explore the idea of a character who is perceived as a different sex than they actually are? Their Mask can absolutely be different than their Mane, because that's an important thing to be able to experience through roleplay, so I really don't care if the book says it should work that way or not. Does the player want to play a character who was secure in their gender identity prior to being taken but having their sex changed in their Durance has left them questioning their identity? It seems like having the Mask and Mane both match their new sex would fit that narrative better, and again I think that narrative is more important than whether the book says that's how it would work or not.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, I don't think there's anything to be ashamed of about asking these kinds of questions. The fact that Changeling allows players to examine issues like the relationship between sex, gender identity, and gender expression, and the experience of those being out-of-synch, is part of what's great about it! So I say good on you for bringing this matter up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 07-24-2015, 12:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T09:58:55-07:00","id":601942,"title":"","content":"Hm... what if someone who was transgender was taken, their sex wasn't changed by it, but when they returned their mask reflected their gender instead of their sex?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T10:07:08-07:00","id":601952,"title":"","content":"I have a Changeling NPC who was male when taken and female when returned. She has a female mask as well as mien (and does identify as female now, though she regards her past self as fully male and herself as transformed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T10:47:07-07:00","id":602011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/601843-biological-sex-and-the-mask?p=601942#post601942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm... what if someone who was transgender was taken, their sex wasn't changed by it, but when they returned their mask reflected their gender instead of their sex?</div> </div> </div> </div>Could definitely be interesting. It would be very much like playing a trans character who has not undergone reassignment surgery, but passed as their gender. I'd certainly allow such a character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T12:33:51-07:00","id":602086,"title":"","content":"I think the answer is perfectly obvious myself: It's different for different Changelings.<br /> <br /> That said if you want to tell a story about Changelings and gender identity you have an enormous elephant in the room. Goblin Markets. If you don't like your biological sex it seems almost obvious that you can buy yourself a sex change (Mein and/or Mask) since the Goblin Markets PDF lists transformations as a category of goods. And there's probably other ways to do it too.<br /> <br /> Changeling is a good game to explore identity issues with, but if you do the transgender charachter who knows what they're supposed to be, the opposite sex, then you have to ask why the Character hasn't just applied a magical solution yet. Changeling and identity works best when after the mind-fuck that is Arcadia you don't know who you are anymore. They are called The Lost after all.<br /> <br /> If you wanted to do a straight forward transgender charachter you'd probably have to be creative. Perhaps the Changeling who's keeper turned him into a woman doesn't want to buy anyone's maleness, he wants <i>his</i> maleness which is unfortunately lying in an Arcadian storage room. Or a Mirrorskin constantly shifted disguises during their Durance but only ever into one sex (long term undercover in a segregated area) and their gender issues isn't that they have the wrong body, since they can shapeshift, it's that they get temporally stuck in the wrong sex whenever they have an Arcadian flashback.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 07-24-2015, 03:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T12:45:08-07:00","id":602116,"title":"","content":"This idea is glorious. What about a keeper who has donned sexes to perform specific roles in his keep and then brought in people who are fitting for that role (say female knights and male stewards for his mansion) and if he finds a guy who'd fit great as a knight, he simply fixes them up, so that their sex matches their role. Hell, I'd even let them marry each other in my keep if I was the keeper and make them swear an oath about it.<br /> Imagine the two of them managing to escape and one of them has been force-gendered into their role. Glorious!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6030-a_newfie","name":"A_Newfie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T21:52:25-07:00","id":602569,"title":"","content":"How about a Keeper who found the most misogynistic, macho man or hateful femi-nazi and changed them just to laugh at their discomfort? To me it seems that the mask should more reflect the creature you have become then the person you where and the differences are part of what makes it near impossible to reclaim the life you lost. As for the transgender person taken and altered, that sounds more like wish fulfillment than tragedy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T22:14:05-07:00","id":602579,"title":"","content":"Wish fufillment isn't a bad idea for a changeling charachter though. Somebody could summon a True Fae because they want a transformation and not realise the cost until it's too late.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T22:19:05-07:00","id":602590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/601843-biological-sex-and-the-mask?p=602569#post602569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the transgender person taken and altered, that sounds more like wish fulfillment than tragedy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Transgender =/= transsexual. Just because a person's gender identity does not match the gender they were assigned at birth does not mean they necessarily want to transition physically. Many trans people are perfectly comfortable with their bodies as they are, and being forcibly altered could be just as traumatic and horrifying for a trans person as it could for a cis person.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T22:42:11-07:00","id":602601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/601843-biological-sex-and-the-mask?p=602086#post602086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the answer is perfectly obvious myself: It's different for different Changelings.<br /> <br /> That said if you want to tell a story about Changelings and gender identity you have an enormous elephant in the room. Goblin Markets. If you don't like your biological sex it seems almost obvious that you can buy yourself a sex change (Mein and/or Mask) since the Goblin Markets PDF lists transformations as a category of goods. And there's probably other ways to do it too.<br /> <br /> Changeling is a good game to explore identity issues with, but if you do the transgender charachter who knows what they're supposed to be, the opposite sex, then you have to ask why the Character hasn't just applied a magical solution yet. Changeling and identity works best when after the mind-fuck that is Arcadia you don't know who you are anymore. They are called The Lost after all.<br /> <br /> If you wanted to do a straight forward transgender charachter you'd probably have to be creative. Perhaps the Changeling who's keeper turned him into a woman doesn't want to buy anyone's maleness, he wants <i>his</i> maleness which is unfortunately lying in an Arcadian storage room. Or a Mirrorskin constantly shifted disguises during their Durance but only ever into one sex (long term undercover in a segregated area) and their gender issues isn't that they have the wrong body, since they can shapeshift, it's that they get temporally stuck in the wrong sex whenever they have an Arcadian flashback.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I honestly didn't know you could do that (blame my lack of the Goblin Markets book). I guess it makes sense? I mean... hrng, gonna have to buy that damn book just so I know what the hell's going on there.<br /> Really not good with Goblin Markets.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Yeah, no mention of that being a service in Core. Is Goblin Markets what I should buy for more information?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6848-taveena","user":"Taveena","date":". 07-25-2015, 01:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6848-taveena","name":"Taveena","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T23:41:35-07:00","id":602641,"title":"","content":"Yes. It doesn't mention anything explicitly about changing sex though, mostly it talks about transformation in terms of extra Kith bonuses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T00:36:57-07:00","id":602690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/601843-biological-sex-and-the-mask?p=602086#post602086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said if you want to tell a story about Changelings and gender identity you have an enormous elephant in the room. Goblin Markets. If you don't like your biological sex it seems almost obvious that you can buy yourself a sex change (Mein and/or Mask) since the Goblin Markets PDF lists transformations as a category of goods. And there's probably other ways to do it too.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the RPG club <b>Changling</b> game I run, I had a very feminine gay player. He wanted to play female character as his RPGer dream, so I let him, even if I pointed to him that there will be &quot;logistic&quot; problems at the LARP-session ( I do not have problems with LGBT issues, I'm bisex bear myself, but I know it works not elegant when other players need to remeber to make all the &quot;he&quot; to &quot;her&quot; and &quot;his&quot; to &quot;hers&quot;, etc. ). After a session, player agreed with me that this was a bad idea and wanted to change his Summer Queen to Summer King. So we made that character get Goblin Contract on the Market to change sex for the price of his memories as female. It was interesting when other PCs where pointing him that he was &quot;Queen&quot; or even imposter to the Summer Crown. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T00:45:53-07:00","id":602693,"title":"","content":"As a general rule, you can buy almost anything imaginable at <i>some</i> goblin market; you just have to find the right seller. Being able to afford what you desire is a different matter entirely, but I'd guess that having your sex permanently changed would cost, at most, the memory of a favorite song, or an irreplaceable but otherwise mundane family heirloom. If you're a skilled haggler, you could probably talk the price down to, say, a wet dream or two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 07-25-2015, 03:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T01:02:46-07:00","id":602703,"title":"","content":"I bought Goblin Markets. WOO I'm a pushover. Anyway- reached the Transformations part of Goblin Markets, and at the moment it's... implied to be pretty damn cheap, assuming that falls under 'permanent cosmetic change'. Rather hard to stretch that out at all. <br /> <br /> The two ideas I've got, as they were, are that either the goblins are heavily inclined to overcharge because of how much it's likely wanted - or the character's Wyrd has become tangled up in their new form. Alternatively it costs more BECAUSE it's inherently valued to the buyer...<br /> <br /> I'd be really interested to hear if you guys have any ways this could actually end up actually being a long-term goal rather than a fairly obvious and immediate purchase.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6848-taveena","name":"Taveena","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T02:59:16-07:00","id":602729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taveena</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/601843-biological-sex-and-the-mask?p=602703#post602703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I bought Goblin Markets. WOO I'm a pushover. Anyway- reached the Transformations part of Goblin Markets, and at the moment it's... implied to be pretty damn cheap, assuming that falls under 'permanent cosmetic change'. Rather hard to stretch that out at all.<br /> <br /> The two ideas I've got, as they were, are that either the goblins are heavily inclined to overcharge because of how much it's likely wanted - or the character's Wyrd has become tangled up in their new form. Alternatively it costs more BECAUSE it's inherently valued to the buyer...<br /> <br /> I'd be really interested to hear if you guys have any ways this could actually end up actually being a long-term goal rather than a fairly obvious and immediate purchase.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say a sex change would be a permanent transformation imitating the Clause Skinmask from the Mirror Contract. I'd use the sugestion made for buying a Kith blessing: pass a kind of trial to be able to take on one's new form. Basically the buyer pay for an opportunity to change sex not the change itself. The market sells a map to a treasure that will change the Changeling, or a chain that will bind and force an exiled Gentry to enact the change.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T09:37:58-07:00","id":603016,"title":"","content":"1) The Goblin Market is intended to generate stories. If you really want to generate a story out of this that way, then make it cost appropriately for the player. That said, consider all the ramifications that come with a person switching their sex outside of the legal process, particularly for people already dislocated. Any attempt to get home will now have a speed bump, and any attempt to make a new life has to contend with some of the added layers of difficulties. Upping the price at the market essentially means that whatever's being paid is the conflict you want to explore over the ones that inherently come with sex-change for the Lost.<br /> <br /> 2) Also on Goblin Markets, I'm pretty sure a sex change is not just a 'permanent cosmetic(read in my mind as surface) change'. There's some internal re-wiring/plumbing that needs to go on too.<br /> <br /> 3) On the Durance as wish fulfillment, it's worth noting that that's actually viable in adjunct with the psychological horror. Remember, one of the things changelings deal with is that the Fae are beautiful as well as terrible, and a large part of their struggle involves learning to appreciate the former when it happens without necessarily tainting it with the latter on instinct.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T10:01:13-07:00","id":603045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/601843-biological-sex-and-the-mask?p=603016#post603016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) The Goblin Market is intended to generate stories. If you really want to generate a story out of this that way, then make it cost appropriately for the player.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm weary of taking this atitude too far as the fundamental building block of all stories is suspension of disbelief. Sacraficing the consistency of the setting for a good story risks undermining that story.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/601843-biological-sex-and-the-mask?p=603016#post603016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) Also on Goblin Markets, I'm pretty sure a sex change is not just a 'permanent cosmetic(read in my mind as surface) change'. There's some internal re-wiring/plumbing that needs to go on too.</div> </div> </div> </div> You get what you pay for. Changlings are sterile anyway so you might be happy with just the externals.<br /> <br /> Or maybe you want to go for the full package that includes unconsious manerisms* or a magical everyone gets my gender right glamour.<br /> <br /> * assuming your unconcious manarisms can even be described as &quot;male&quot; or &quot;female&quot; instead of &quot;Ogre&quot; or &quot;Wizened&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T10:31:32-07:00","id":603063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/601843-biological-sex-and-the-mask?p=603016#post603016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) On the Durance as wish fulfillment, it's worth noting that that's actually viable in adjunct with the psychological horror. Remember, one of the things changelings deal with is that the Fae are beautiful as well as terrible, and a large part of their struggle involves learning to appreciate the former when it happens without necessarily tainting it with the latter on instinct.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, wish fullfilment gone wrong is a staple of fairy tales. Plenty of story material there.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T10:35:29-07:00","id":603064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/601843-biological-sex-and-the-mask?p=603045#post603045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm weary of taking this atitude too far as the fundamental building block of all stories is suspension of disbelief. Sacraficing the consistency of the setting for a good story risks undermining that story.</div> </div> </div> </div>When the setting is essentially half-storytelling incarnate, maintaining consistency of the setting means shifting the standards for a good story. Changeling is a game where the setting half-flows around people, places, times, and ideas with greater narrative gravitas than others. This is most prominent in Arcadia(see Seemings, and yes, I know your stance, and yes, I think you're wrong, and yes, I know you think I'm wrong, moving on), but the Hedge certainly contains strong touches of that, and certainly that comes out the most in Goblin Markets. Hell, the supplement says as much.<br /> <br /> Changeling is a fluid setting. Take advantage of it and use it to the fullest.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T12:19:54-07:00","id":603102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/601843-biological-sex-and-the-mask?p=601942#post601942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm... what if someone who was transgender was taken, their sex wasn't changed by it, but when they returned their mask reflected their gender instead of their sex?</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I don't think that could happen. The Mask is sophisticated and thorough, but it's not very smart. If the body says &quot;I am a boy,&quot; then the Mask says &quot;yep.&quot; If your character is sexless, the Mask asks itself if the character is more manlike or womanlike, and creates a suitable appearance. If your character is something really out there, like a futanari, the Mask creates a matching appearance, which will give a doctor whanging headaches.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T12:26:27-07:00","id":603105,"title":"","content":"Do hermaphrodites cause doctors whanging headaches?<br /> <br /> But yeah, the Mask covers what's there. It interacts with the perceptions of others in accordance to the promises made by the Wyrd-forged form/body and delivers accordingly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T13:04:17-07:00","id":603154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/601843-biological-sex-and-the-mask?p=603105#post603105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do hermaphrodites cause doctors whanging headaches?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sure you didn't mean it this way, but hermaphrodite is actually a wildly offensive term. Intersex is more appropriate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T13:17:26-07:00","id":603157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/601843-biological-sex-and-the-mask?p=603154#post603154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sure you didn't mean it this way, but hermaphrodite is actually a wildly offensive term. Intersex is more appropriate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not trying to say one should use an offensive appellation, but hermaphrodism is just a one of the numerous intersexed conditions though. It seems a bit imprecise to use Intersex when it coud refer to so many others conditions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T13:19:20-07:00","id":603158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/601843-biological-sex-and-the-mask?p=603105#post603105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do hermaphrodites cause doctors whanging headaches?<br /> <br /> But yeah, the Mask covers what's there. It interacts with the perceptions of others in accordance to the promises made by the Wyrd-forged form/body and delivers accordingly.</div> </div> </div> </div>A hentai-style futanari would indeed give a doctor whanging headaches; such a person simply shouldn't be possible. I'm quite aware of intersexed people, but futanari aren't that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T13:26:49-07:00","id":603161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/601843-biological-sex-and-the-mask?p=603154#post603154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sure you didn't mean it this way, but hermaphrodite is actually a wildly offensive term. Intersex is more appropriate.</div> </div> </div> </div>This, I have not heard before. If you could me a favor and shoot me a PM explaining why, that'd be appreciated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T14:20:07-07:00","id":603191,"title":"","content":"I've not heard that either. Hermaphrodie would be inaccurate for real life human biology but I've not heard it being offensive either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T14:32:41-07:00","id":603197,"title":"","content":"I'm not intersex myself, so I don't speak with any kind of experience or authority on the matter, but as I understand it, it's clinically inaccurate, and has often been used in to refer to intersex people in a negative context, or as an insult. <a href=\"http://www.isna.org/faq/hermaphrodite\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> is a link to the Intersex Society of North America's FAQ entry on the use of hermaphrodite and derived words.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T14:52:26-07:00","id":603218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/601843-biological-sex-and-the-mask?p=603197#post603197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not intersex myself, so I don't speak with any kind of experience or authority on the matter, but as I understand it, it's clinically inaccurate, and has often been used in to refer to intersex people in a negative context, or as an insult. <a href=\"http://www.isna.org/faq/hermaphrodite\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> is a link to the Intersex Society of North America's FAQ entry on the use of hermaphrodite and derived words.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T15:13:23-07:00","id":603236,"title":"","content":"So, question: Changeling is a setting where someone can be...well, not totally impossible, but the impossible within the human form. In other words, a changeling could be an actual hermaphrodite.<br /> <br /> ....I'm not sure where my question went, but basically it's along the lines of &quot;So, if a character is an actual hermaphrodite, is it still a problem?&quot;, to which is the answer is probably &quot;Probably not, but be very careful how you play it and what sort of stories you tell with it.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T15:17:12-07:00","id":603239,"title":"","content":"Given that the Vampire Gameline is essentially about playing abusers, I can hardly see how playing a hermaphrodite would be worse. There's also playable Mage legacy that's described as being hermaphrodites.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 07-25-2015, 06:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T15:59:32-07:00","id":603262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/601843-biological-sex-and-the-mask?p=603236#post603236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, question: Changeling is a setting where someone can be...well, not totally impossible, but the impossible within the human form. In other words, a changeling could be an actual hermaphrodite.<br /> <br /> ....I'm not sure where my question went, but basically it's along the lines of &amp;quot;So, if a character is an actual hermaphrodite, is it still a problem?&amp;quot;, to which is the answer is probably &amp;quot;Probably not, but be very careful how you play it and what sort of stories you tell with it.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds about right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T22:12:59-07:00","id":603503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/601843-biological-sex-and-the-mask?p=603102#post603102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I don't think that could happen. The Mask is sophisticated and thorough, but it's not very smart. If the body says &quot;I am a boy,&quot; then the Mask says &quot;yep.&quot; If your character is sexless, the Mask asks itself if the character is more manlike or womanlike, and creates a suitable appearance. If your character is something really out there, like a futanari, the Mask creates a matching appearance, which will give a doctor whanging headaches.</div> </div> </div> </div>For what it's worth, the aforementioned Bodhisattvas can end up with a mien with a different sex to their mask.<br /> <br /> Also while I'm similarly not intersexed (shockingly, given a concept based on heavy binarism), it's pretty hard to find a term that is... unambiguously inoffensive - 'hermaphrodite' is inaccurate, archaic, and has history as a slur, 'intersexed' is somewhat inaccurate (it's not like they're halfway between an X and a Y chromosome, after all), 'disorders in sex development' has a negative and cissexist stigma. 'Intersexed' is the default because its judgment of normativity is somewhat downplayed compared to DSD and it doesn't have a history of use as a slur (or as fetish art) like 'futa' and 'hermaphrodite' do. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6848-taveena","name":"Taveena","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T23:19:40-07:00","id":603538,"title":"","content":"*Intersex. It's an adjective, not an adverb. And since it's the term generally used <i>by most intersex people</i>, you can safely assume it's the most inoffensive term to use. Obviously, you can't use labels without the risk of offending <i>someone</i>, but if you use the term that members of the group in question generally prefer, you'll be fine. If someone of that group specifically tells you they don't care for that term, you can simply apologize and ask if there's something else they would rather you refer to them as.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, about the chromosome thing? Yeah, it may be more common for men to have XY chromosomes and women to have XX chromosomes, but there are actually plenty of individuals who break that trend, both trans and cis. One of the people in my old college LARP troupe was an XX cis man.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 07-26-2015, 02:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T23:23:20-07:00","id":603541,"title":"","content":"It's funny, I was introduced to hermaphroditism in terms of it as a sacred concept or icon. It's going to take me some to spin the idea around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T23:58:03-07:00","id":603583,"title":"","content":"Naturally, different cultures be different.<br /> <br /> It's both a sacred concept and icon and a medically inaccurate and offensive term depending on where in the world you are. Learning the list of who thinks what about the word is far less important than just generally keeping an open mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T00:21:30-07:00","id":603589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/601843-biological-sex-and-the-mask?p=603583#post603583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Naturally, different cultures be different.<br /> <br /> It's both a sacred concept and icon and a medically inaccurate and offensive term depending on where in the world you are. Learning the list of who thinks what about the word is far less important than just generally keeping an open mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well said.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T03:03:53-07:00","id":603698,"title":"","content":"This thread makes me think of this character...<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://img1.wikia.nocookie.net/__cb20110629082940/steins-gate/images/8/8e/Ruka_profile.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Steins; Gate. Watch it and imagine them being Changelings and the best anime I've ever seen in my life just became better.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6030-a_newfie","name":"A_Newfie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T05:24:44-07:00","id":603744,"title":"","content":"What do you mean it's impossible for them to have biological sex? They can have sex, it's just that most of them can't produce children. Actually that's not entirely true, I remember reading something that said like 1% of the Changeling population can still have kids, and there are also special contracts that allow you to do so, but the kids are born human with the possibility of being Fae Touched.<br /> <br /> Or maybe I'm completely wrong and the new rewrite for Fae Touched changed this?<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> <br /> Wait, I get it now, you were asking about gender roles. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Actually in the first edition, it clearly said that a Changeling's fae appearance is reduced after returning to the mortal world. An Elemental, for example, doesn't remain an animated snow sculpture, but they would have the characteristics of snow about them. A cold personality, snow crystals peppering their skin, est. But their body would mostly return to a human shape.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind, I don't know if this remains the case in 2nd edition, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 07-26-2015, 03:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T06:06:07-07:00","id":603784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/601843-biological-sex-and-the-mask?p=603744#post603744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you mean it's impossible for them to have biological sex? They can have sex, it's just that most of them can't produce children. Actually that's not entirely true, I remember reading something that said like 1% of the Changeling population can still have kids, and there are also special contracts that allow you to do so, but the kids are born human with the possibility of being Fae Touched.<br /> <br /> Or maybe I'm completely wrong and the new rewrite for Fae Touched changed this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Really?<br /> To quote Arcane Arts, does this mean that someone born a man then changed by their keeper could in theory come back to the mundane world and end up pregnant? O.o","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6030-a_newfie","name":"A_Newfie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T07:57:35-07:00","id":603805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/601843-biological-sex-and-the-mask?p=603744#post603744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, I get it now, you were asking about gender roles. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>No, we're talking about sex. There is a difference between sex and gender. Sex is what parts you have, gender is your identity along the spectrum of &quot;maleness&quot; and &quot;femaleness&quot;. Gender roles are social constructs based on cultural ideals of what maleness and femaleness imply and how men and women &quot;should&quot; fit into society.<br /> <br /> What's interesting about Changeling is that the split between Mask and Mane can be used as a metaphor for the split between sex and gender expression.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T09:26:34-07:00","id":603890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A_Newfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/601843-biological-sex-and-the-mask?p=603784#post603784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Really?<br /> To quote Arcane Arts, does this mean that someone born a man then changed by their keeper could in theory come back to the mundane world and end up pregnant? O.o</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think I ever said that. And, provided sterility from the Fae hasn't kicked in, the answer is yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T10:35:05-07:00","id":603933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/601843-biological-sex-and-the-mask?p=603890#post603890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think I ever said that. And, provided sterility from the Fae hasn't kicked in, the answer is yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I mean, you said that there's a small chance someone who was been stolen to the fae realm could still be fertile.<br /> The rest of the bits was just me drawing my own conclusions.<br /> With your wise words of fixed/changed plumbing.<br /> <br /> <b>Awesome!</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6030-a_newfie","name":"A_Newfie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T10:54:20-07:00","id":603945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/601843-biological-sex-and-the-mask?p=603805#post603805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, we're talking about sex. There is a difference between sex and gender. Sex is what parts you have, gender is your identity along the spectrum of &quot;maleness&quot; and &quot;femaleness&quot;. Gender roles are social constructs based on cultural ideals of what maleness and femaleness imply and how men and women &quot;should&quot; fit into society.<br /> <br /> What's interesting about Changeling is that the split between Mask and Mane can be used as a metaphor for the split between sex and gender expression.</div> </div> </div> </div>Grrr, I want to be able to like more than once!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6030-a_newfie","name":"A_Newfie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T12:45:00-07:00","id":604029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/601843-biological-sex-and-the-mask?p=602693#post602693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a general rule, you can buy almost anything imaginable at <i>some</i> goblin market; you just have to find the right seller. Being able to afford what you desire is a different matter entirely, but I'd guess that having your sex permanently changed would cost, at most, the memory of a favorite song, or an irreplaceable but otherwise mundane family heirloom. If you're a skilled haggler, you could probably talk the price down to, say, a wet dream or two.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I was watching a live play on youtube where they bought a calculator that warned you of impending death and all the merchant wanted in exchange was the first smile of an infant child. The players started looking for a bin full of severed baby heads!<br /> <br /> <br /> On another note, this topic has given me an amusing mental image of an Ogre wanting to be pretty, so they try to become a girl, along with hilarious consequences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 07-26-2015, 03:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T13:30:08-07:00","id":604059,"title":"","content":"I know no one has to be reminded Transgender people are indeed a real thing, but please bear that in mind when making comments. I am not calling anyone out here, just reminding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T14:07:45-07:00","id":604132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A_Newfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/601843-biological-sex-and-the-mask?p=603933#post603933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, I mean, you said that there's a small chance someone who was been stolen to the fae realm could still be fertile.<br /> The rest of the bits was just me drawing my own conclusions.<br /> With your wise words of fixed/changed plumbing.<br /> <br /> <b>Awesome!</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Changelings can get around their infertility, but most methods are dangerous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T14:09:32-07:00","id":604133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baron Samedi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/601843-biological-sex-and-the-mask?p=604059#post604059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know no one has to be reminded Transgender people are indeed a real thing, but please bear that in mind when making comments. I am not calling anyone out here, just reminding.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not only that, there are a fair few transgender people who frequent these forums. I myself am genderfluid, which is part of the trans spectrum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T21:52:49-07:00","id":605289,"title":"","content":"Bein' trans is - I mean, I think, I'm not a neuropsychologist with access to my entire mental history - a big part of WHY I'm so interested in this story. Before I transitioned it was wish-fulfillment (and it still is, because I am a bundle of barely functional neuroses) and it never really stopped. <br /> <br /> It's tricky though - there are... a few aspects of it. The first is that I want the character to be changed unwillingly - I've played characters who WANTED to be changed, but they ran out of steam really fast, because ultimately I didn't... know how to play a trans character whose dysphoria had been resolved. There wasn't really any arc there, so it's got to go fish-out-of-water. Second is that it needs to be a STRUGGLE to get back - again, because otherwise the story ends too fast and I'm left with a character I don't know how to play. Third is that they DO need to go back - as mentioned, I'm trans, and if they DON'T want to go back, then that implies the mind is a plaything of the body and that gender is a product of biological sex, which... is not something pleasant to think about. I tend to play characters who identify as male - even though I don't - because that means the transformation also acts as wish fulfillment (for me, not them). And then the reaffirmation of their gender - the continuous desire to return to being male - while somewhat out of character, is also slightly DISTANCED from me, which makes it a little easier to deal with.<br /> <br /> So I'm trying to write a character arc that includes all those elements. And as a result of the discussion in the thread, it currently seems like number 2 is the hardest, though...<br /> <br /> I mean, the example for 'permanent cosmetic changes' is a change of haircolor, and a rewrite of someone's entire biological sex seems somewhat beyond that level. (... Also, given how Goblin Markets work, it doesn't seem impossible that sex would be the ONLY thing that's changed, resulting in them still APPEARING female. Getting a Y chromosome back doesn't necessitate the sudden disappearance of female secondary sexual characteristics. Or primary.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6848-taveena","name":"Taveena","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T07:27:48-07:00","id":605561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taveena</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/601843-biological-sex-and-the-mask?p=605289#post605289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bein' trans is - I mean, I think, I'm not a neuropsychologist with access to my entire mental history - a big part of WHY I'm so interested in this story. Before I transitioned it was wish-fulfillment (and it still is, because I am a bundle of barely functional neuroses) and it never really stopped.<br /> <br /> It's tricky though - there are... a few aspects of it. The first is that I want the character to be changed unwillingly - I've played characters who WANTED to be changed, but they ran out of steam really fast, because ultimately I didn't... know how to play a trans character whose dysphoria had been resolved. There wasn't really any arc there, so it's got to go fish-out-of-water. Second is that it needs to be a STRUGGLE to get back - again, because otherwise the story ends too fast and I'm left with a character I don't know how to play. Third is that they DO need to go back - as mentioned, I'm trans, and if they DON'T want to go back, then that implies the mind is a plaything of the body and that gender is a product of biological sex, which... is not something pleasant to think about. I tend to play characters who identify as male - even though I don't - because that means the transformation also acts as wish fulfillment (for me, not them). And then the reaffirmation of their gender - the continuous desire to return to being male - while somewhat out of character, is also slightly DISTANCED from me, which makes it a little easier to deal with.<br /> <br /> So I'm trying to write a character arc that includes all those elements. And as a result of the discussion in the thread, it currently seems like number 2 is the hardest, though...<br /> <br /> I mean, the example for 'permanent cosmetic changes' is a change of haircolor, and a rewrite of someone's entire biological sex seems somewhat beyond that level. (... Also, given how Goblin Markets work, it doesn't seem impossible that sex would be the ONLY thing that's changed, resulting in them still APPEARING female. Getting a Y chromosome back doesn't necessitate the sudden disappearance of female secondary sexual characteristics. Or primary.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I don't know if you've ever read the comic Twokinds, but there's a character named Natani who has the body of a female but the soul of a male. The short version of the backstory is that there are a pair of siblings, Natani and Zen who went on a mission that ended horribly. In order to save each other, Natani and Zen allowed their souls to be merged into the same body. Natani was the sister, and Zen was the brother. The process left Natani with a male gender identity and he responds quite aggressively to those who attempt to point out that his body is clearly that of a woman's.<br /> <br /> <br /> To minimize this, Natani used methods to disguise himself like a man. Taping down his breasts, bathing alone, est. His gender was finally discovered when he accidentally entered the bath, thinking it was empty and one of his companions saw him naked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 07-28-2015, 10:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T10:06:45-07:00","id":605676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/601843-biological-sex-and-the-mask?p=605561#post605561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know if you've ever read the comic Twokinds, but there's a character named Natani who has the body of a female but the soul of a male. The short version of the backstory is that there are a pair of siblings, Natani and Zen who went on a mission that ended horribly. In order to save each other, Natani and Zen allowed their souls to be merged into the same body. Natani was the sister, and Zen was the brother. The process left Natani with a male gender identity and he responds quite aggressively to those who attempt to point out that his body is clearly that of a woman's.<br /> <br /> To minimize this, Natani used methods to disguise himself like a man. Taping down his breasts, bathing alone, est. His gender was finally discovered when he accidentally entered the bath, thinking it was empty and one of his companions saw him naked.</div> </div> </div> </div>If he's a man, any body he has is a man's body, because it's his and he's a man. It's just a man's body that happens to have breasts and a uterus and doesn't have a penis. Though I suppose in this case it is his sister's body, not his. Nonetheless, the whole &quot;x trapped in a y's body&quot; narrative is very misleading. I would have come to terms with my gender identity much sooner in life if I hadn't had this misconception that all trans people necessarily feel &quot;trapped&quot; or &quot;wrong&quot; in their bodies.<br /> <br /> Likewise, he's not disguising himself as a man, because he is a man. He's just trying to express his gender in a way that makes him feel more comfortable and minimizes risk of other people mistaking him for a woman based on his appearance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T12:43:01-07:00","id":605841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/601843-biological-sex-and-the-mask?p=605676#post605676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If he's a man, any body he has is a man's body, because it's his and he's a man. It's just a man's body that happens to have breasts and a uterus and doesn't have a penis. Though I suppose in this case it is his sister's body, not his. Nonetheless, the whole &quot;x trapped in a y's body&quot; narrative is very misleading. I would have come to terms with my gender identity much sooner in life if I hadn't had this misconception that all trans people necessarily feel &quot;trapped&quot; or &quot;wrong&quot; in their bodies.<br /> <br /> Likewise, he's not disguising himself as a man, because he is a man. He's just trying to express his gender in a way that makes him feel more comfortable and minimizes risk of other people mistaking him for a woman based on his appearance.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. This comic is literally about a guy stuck in a woman's body. The narrative may be different somewhere else, but in the context of Twokinds, it is <u>literally</u> about being trapped in another body and disguising himself. I understand where you are coming from and what point you are trying to make, but what you are saying is incorrect in the context of Twokinds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6030-a_newfie","name":"A_Newfie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T14:54:17-07:00","id":605964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A_Newfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/601843-biological-sex-and-the-mask?p=605841#post605841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No. This comic is literally about a guy stuck in a woman's body. The narrative may be different somewhere else, but in the context of Twokinds, it is <u>literally</u> about being trapped in another body and disguising himself. I understand where you are coming from and what point you are trying to make, but what you are saying is incorrect in the context of Twokinds.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As I said, their souls were merged into the same body. Natani's body ended up being the host, but Zen became the dominate personality. Anyways, the point of my above post was to provide a possible idea for the character to be portrayed in the game. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T18:35:26-07:00","id":606126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A_Newfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/601843-biological-sex-and-the-mask?p=605841#post605841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No. This comic is literally about a guy stuck in a woman's body. The narrative may be different somewhere else, but in the context of Twokinds, it is <u>literally</u> about being trapped in another body and disguising himself. I understand where you are coming from and what point you are trying to make, but what you are saying is incorrect in the context of Twokinds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you miss the part where I acknowledged &quot;Though I guess in this case it is his sister's body, not his&quot; and then went on to explain why the &quot;in the wrong body&quot; narrative in general is problematic as a representation of a trans character?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T04:04:12-07:00","id":606468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/601843-biological-sex-and-the-mask?p=605964#post605964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> As I said, their souls were merged into the same body. Natani's body ended up being the host, but Zen became the dominate personality. Anyways, the point of my above post was to provide a possible idea for the character to be portrayed in the game. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I quite liked it. I wonder if Keepers with their (close to) divine powers could do something similar, like squeezing the personality out of one person and into another, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6030-a_newfie","name":"A_Newfie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T05:58:37-07:00","id":606507,"title":"","content":"Of course they could.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T08:08:08-07:00","id":606591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A_Newfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/601843-biological-sex-and-the-mask?p=606468#post606468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I quite liked it. I wonder if Keepers with their (close to) divine powers could do something similar, like squeezing the personality out of one person and into another, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> 1st edition allowed them to turn you into a mountain or a lightning bolt or even the sky itself. Putting you in another body seems like child's play compared to that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T08:09:02-07:00","id":606593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/601843-biological-sex-and-the-mask?p=606507#post606507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course they could.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean... it's complicated, isn't it? Keepers can play with their minds to a pretty large degree but ultimately their minds ARE reclaimed - s'the 1e Beast narrative. <br /> It's... messy? If that happened then when they escaped they'd presumably... end up back in their own body, or...<br /> <br /> It gets WEIRD when Keepers aren't flat-up turning Changelings into inhuman monsters, because while it's pretty obvious that the Ogre is likely just a burlier version of how they used to be... this kind of thing results in... you looking like you did before, but... more like the person whose body you were transplanted into?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6848-taveena","name":"Taveena","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T08:18:58-07:00","id":606628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taveena</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/601843-biological-sex-and-the-mask?p=606593#post606593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It gets WEIRD when Keepers aren't flat-up turning Changelings into inhuman monsters, because while it's pretty obvious that the Ogre is likely just a burlier version of how they used to be... this kind of thing results in... you looking like you did before, but... more like the person whose body you were transplanted into?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we've finally uncovered the shocking backstory behind David Bowie.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}